#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# input_form

#% text
# `input_form(x)` shows `x` in the input syntax, as text that reads back as the same term.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The argument is evaluated first; `input_form` stays around the value as a wrapper that changes only how it is shown.

#% item
# Values are already shown in the input syntax, so `input_form` matters where a front end typesets output.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
input_form(x + y^2)
#% output
#= x + y^2

#% cell
input_form([1/2, a*b])
#% output
#= [1/2, a*b]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `full_form` shows the plain calls instead:

#% cell
full_form(x + y^2)
#% output
#= add(x, pow(y, 2))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `full_form`, `to_string`
